25,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The earth-moving firms are worried about clay and slippage. However, we can hoard the southern area in stages without closing the whole park.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Most people just use the park as a shortcut to the tram, sticking to firm ground. Also, drainage is failing and the heat is intense.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Minato,,"Our staff numbers have dropped a lot, but we have great volunteers for habitat work and youth sports.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The old overflow basin is still perfect, but the paved areas are crumbling. Also, many new trees died because of poor aftercare.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The habitat fund covers planting and water, but nothing else. Meanwhile, maintaining greenery is now three times more expensive than hard surfaces.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if people are sticking to firm ground, maybe we should avoid too many soft paths?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly, Kenji. And with the drainage issues, we can't just ignore the water management.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, does the habitat fund make planting more attractive even if the upkeep is expensive?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, I'm worried about the upkeep. If the trees died before, will expensive maintenance actually save them this time?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a risk, Minato. The fund helps the start, but the city pays the long-term bill, which is rising.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Minako, if the basin held up but the pavement didn't, maybe we should trust the water-based engineering more?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,That's a logical point. But we must ensure the design doesn't fight the tram-commuter flow.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Minato,,I'm glad we have volunteers for sports and habitats. That might offset the staff shortage.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Minako,,I still distrust the planting records. We need something that doesn't require a miracle to survive.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Minako. We should be wary of anything that creates a massive, permanent financial drain on the ledger.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
