49,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"The options are A: Wetland Restoration, B: Market Plaza, C: Woodland Walk, and D: Sports Terraces. I like A or D.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"B and D suit the commuter flow, but A addresses the drainage and heat issues I found.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Minato,,A and D both have volunteer support. I think D would be very lively!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Minako,,C is too risky given the tree death records. B's paving might crumble like the civic hall apron.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A is funded by the habitat fund, but the upkeep is triple that of B or D.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, but A uses the fund for the big costs. @Benjamin, would the boardwalks in A interfere with the tram walkers?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Probably not, as long as the main paths stay firm. But D's running loop is very efficient for movement.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, would the sports terraces be easier to maintain than a forest?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Minako,,Likely yes. Harder surfaces and managed courts are more predictable than a woodland.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,D seems the most fiscally stable. It avoids the high upkeep of A and C.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about the clay slippage for A. D is in the south, which I found is easier to hoard and build.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,That's a strong point. D fits the usage patterns and the construction constraints.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Minato,,I really like D! The youth league volunteers would be so happy.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Minako,,D is the most pragmatic. It avoids the failures I saw in the planting and paving records.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. D is the most sustainable choice for the city's budget.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for D!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Minato,,D for me too!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Minako,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
